    "baseline_explanation": "This passage highlights a key design choice in DiaryMate’s \"Recommending next sentences\" feature. Instead of pushing a single, automated continuation for the user to blindly accept, the system generates five different candidate sentences based on what the user has already written. This design matters because personal journaling is a deeply subjective and reflective task. By presenting a variety of choices—which users can further customize by adjusting a \"temperature\" slider to get more typical or unique sentences—the system shifts the AI's role from an authoritative writer to an exploratory brainstorming partner. It invites users to actively compare different tones, perspectives, and directions for their entries. This connects directly to the paper's main focus on the balance of agency in Human-AI collaborative writing. While the researchers designed this multi-option feature to help users reflect and maintain control over their narratives, their findings later show a complex tension: while it successfully helped users view their experiences from new perspectives, it also occasionally led to over-reliance, where users favored the AI's polished emotional expressions over their own authentic voice."
